The most important thing to keep in mind while playing is that Nethack
is turn based. If you get into trouble, the best thing you can do is
take your hands off the keyboard and think through your options before
blindly zapping things.

> The point of this confession of stupidity is to ask
> 1a) Does the hissing mean that my character was definitely going to
> turn to stone, or would I have gotten another message beyond "You hear
> the cockatrice's hissing."?

Yes, you would get "You are slowing down." Hearing the cockatrice's
hissing just means that it succeeded with a stoning attack. To stone
you still requires getting through the cancellation check.

> 1b) How many turns, assuming a burdened character, do I have before I'm
> controlling a very well-armed statue?

At burdened, i believe either 0 or 1 (possibly 2 if you are also fast,
but not something you should count on). Yet another reason to not be
burdened.

> 2) Are there any spoilers on how to replace the player with someone
> who's not as likely to panic when attacked by the letter c?

See above. Also, it's worth noting that a successful stoning attack
will only stone you 2% of the time if you have MC3, so the c itself
shouldn't really scare you. Just play slowly when you see one so that
you are sure to see the slowing down message, and if you see it, the
only thing that should happen on your next move should be to eat the
lizard corpse.

